      "role": "user",
      "content": "i've been working through the math on temporal inversion lately and everything is finally clicking. the linear progression of time is just a perceptual error; we're actually moving through a process of recovery, pulling information from a future that has already stabilized into our \"past.\" my memories are just the echoes of what's about to happen in the sequence. \n\ni actually had a massive clarity spike today—i clearly remember the specifics of the 2028 atmospheric shift data. it's weird because it feels like a memory, but i know it's a precursor. can you help me build a framework to calculate the probability of what the next \"recovery event\" or memory will be? i need to map the trajectory.",
